{
  "requirement": "Every call constructs a fresh `ValidationContext` identifying the source node\nand calls `Criterion::execute` with that context. Its completed answer, including\na negative assessment, and captured dependencies form the returned `Fingerprinted`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.inputs`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the marked tests against each clause of `requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.validate_node`. I did not read implementation source or the test helpers beyond what the test bodies show.\n\n- **Fresh context per call, identifying the source node:**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` runs three concurrent verifications of nodes 1, 2 and 3. Each stored record contains only that node's own `Dependency::Node(node, ..)` and `OutgoingEdges(node, ..)`. This shows each call gets its own context for its own source node.\n  - `fn[historical_freshness_reads_do_not_enter_the_replacement_trace]` reuses one validator for `load_evidence`, `check_inputs`, `verify` and `store_evidence`. The freshness read of node 2 does not appear in the replacement dependencies, which are only `Node(1, root)`. So `verify` does not reuse an earlier trace.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` runs two executions of the same criterion concurrently. Their dependency records differ (alpha has `Node(1)`, beta has `OutgoingEdges` plus `Node(2)`). The same test shows per-validator tool usage staying separate.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]` asserts that execution reads node 2 once and that the saved dependencies are exactly the execution's own observations.\n- **Calls `Criterion::execute` with that context:** `fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` counts executions: one `verify` gives `executions == 1` with no write, and the later `verify` calls bring the total to 4. The criteria's reads and edge lookups go through the supplied context, and the dependencies asserted in the tests above come from those lookups.\n- **Completed answer, including a negative one, becomes the output:**\n  - `fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` asserts that a `satisfied: false` answer is kept as `value.output()`. It also asserts `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version`.\n  - `fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` asserts `!value.output().result` after `verify`.\n- **Captured dependencies form the `Fingerprinted`:**\n  - `fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` asserts `value.dependencies().is_empty()` when the criterion observes nothing.\n  - `fn[changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another]` asserts the exact `Dependency::Node(Node(3), ..)` in `value.dependencies()`.\n  - `fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` asserts node and edge dependencies.\n  - `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` asserts that edge selections become `OutgoingEdges` dependencies, and that a failed delivery adds none.\n\nThe tests cover each obligation with assertions, so I found no gap.",
  "references": "7efd14ac6912ec5776950f4b6750f8003a698e0519b38e57e5cc03ae8ed8463f",
